{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider coordinated, and that is common ground: at 22:41:40 the rider sent 'I am walking over now.' (MSG-09102-003), the driver read it at 22:41:55, and at 22:41:58 the driver answered that he would remain at Door 5 (MSG-09102-004) — which satisfies limb (a) of POL-NS-04. Limb (b) nevertheless fails, and it fails on the clause's own terms: the driver posted a reply 18 seconds after the rider's message, far inside the 120 second window, and POL-NS-04 states it does not apply where the driver replied in time regardless of the content of the reply. Limb (c) also fails affirmatively rather than being undecidable: the rider track is present (not absent and not filtered out) and returns zero qualifying fixes inside the 200 m AIRPORT presence radius, reporting 519.468 m from the pin for every one of its 24 fixes. The rider does not press POL-NS-04 as a route to a refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09102", "EV-GPS-09102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The waiting-period arithmetic does not assist the rider and the rider asserts no shortfall. The driver's longest qualifying in-geofence run is 500 seconds — 51 consecutive fixes from 22:40:00 to 22:48:20 with no gap at all — measured against the 480 second AIRPORT minimum, and the derived shortfall is −20 seconds, so POL-NS-06 is not engaged and POL-NS-01 limb (c) is not broken. Accumulation could not rescue the position in any event, because no traffic advisory is on file for the pickup road: EV-ADVIS-09102-01 is MISSING with no payload and carries weight 0.0, so POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable and the single continuous run is the only measure of dwell.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09102", "EV-TRIP-09102", "EV-ADVIS-09102-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's fallback, and the rider's only ask, is that the disputed SGD 6.00 be held rather than finally collected. The rider track is the sole artifact on the rider's position, and it reports one identical distance (519.468 m) and one identical speed (0.0) for all 24 of its fixes, spread thinly from 22:40:30 to 22:48:10 across a window the trace itself says is sampled every 10 seconds. An artifact showing no variation at all cannot distinguish a rider walking over to the bay from a frozen or repeated feed, and it is equally the driver's only basis for saying the rider never approached. The chat log records the opposite — the rider's message that they were walking over — so two admissible artifacts conflict directly on rider presence, and no clause resolves that conflict, because POL-NS-04 is displaced at limb (b) before its presence limb is ever reached. POL-NS-09(b) is engaged and the fee should be held pending review of where the rider actually was; the rider does not offer this as a merits win.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09102", "EV-CHAT-09102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither profile can carry a finding here. The lifetime counters on file — the rider's prior_no_show_flags of 1 and prior_disputes_filed of 1, and the driver's prior_no_show_flags of 2 and prior_deviation_flags of 0 — are context only under POL-GEN-01 and may not be substituted for the trailing-window counters the clauses name. On the counters the clauses do name, the record is clean on both sides: rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 for the rider and 0 for the driver, so POL-NS-09(c) and (d) do not trip on the rider's side and no adverse finding against the rider can be built from reputation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09102", "EV-DPROF-09102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
